 "key_big": "Same signs: positive. Different signs: negative.",
 "key_sub": "Count the negative signs: even is positive, odd is negative.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Same signs: the product or quotient is <b>positive</b>. (−6) × (−4) = 24.</li><li>Different signs: the product or quotient is <b>negative</b>. 18 ÷ (−3) = −6.</li><li>With many factors, count the negative signs: an even number gives a positive answer, an odd number a negative answer.</li><li>Check a division with multiplication: (−6) × (−3) = 18.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>(−2) × 3 × (−5)</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>two negatives: positive</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 30</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Two negatives make a negative</td><td>(−3) × (−4) = 12.</td></tr><tr><td>Sign of a quotient</td><td>−20 ÷ 4 = −5.</td></tr><tr><td>Counting signs</td><td>Three negative factors give a negative product.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does MATATAG Math 7 ask about multiplying integers?",
   "a": "Multiply and divide integers."
  },
  {
   "q": "Why is a negative times a negative positive?",
   "a": "Taking away negative groups is like adding positive ones."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is −24 ÷ (−6)?",
   "a": "4."
  },
  {
   "q": "Can I divide by 0?",
   "a": "No. Division by 0 is undefined."
  }
